OL,3,GNEWSAThe druid, the weather presenter
OL,4,Aand the astronomer - when does autumn
OL,5,Astart?
OL,6,
OL,7,FFor most of us, autumn means falling
OL,8,Fleaves, shorter days, returning to
OL,9,Fschool and the more modern tradition of
OL,10,Fpumpkin spice lattes popping up again.
OL,12,FBut when does it officially begin? Well
OL,13,Fthat depends on which calendar you
OL,14,Ffollow.
OL,16,FMany will argue 1 September is the day
OL,17,Fthe seasons change, and they are right
OL,18,Faccording to the meteorological
OL,19,Fcalendar.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,419,410,260,120,0,100
